# Pesto input-filter reference.
# Pesto does not load .env files or read ext/exclude from environment variables.
# Put the following TOML keys in config.toml BEFORE its first section instead.
# Copy config.example.toml for a complete configuration, then pass it with:
#   pesto --config /path/to/config.toml /path/to/Release/
#
# TOML example (these comments are not environment-variable assignments):
#   ext = []
#   exclude = [".courseid", "*.tmp", "*.log"]
#   no_exclude = false
#
# ext = [] allows all extensions, including files without an extension.
# To allow only selected extensions, use ext = ["mkv", "mp4", "srt", "nfo"].
# Extension matching is case-insensitive; ext also applies to explicit files.
#
# exclude adds case-sensitive globs to the default OS/FUSE exclusions.
# Hidden .courseid files are included by default; the example excludes them.
# Basename globs match at any depth. Path globs are relative to each input
# directory, using / separators. Matching directories prune the whole subtree.
# Explicit file arguments bypass exclusions, but still obey ext.
#
# no_exclude = true disables default and custom exclusions; ext still applies.
# CLI --ext and --exclude replace their respective custom config lists.
# Full matching rules: crates/pesto/README.md, "Directory exclusions".
